# Credentials (never commit)
credentials.env
# credentials.env.example is deliberately NOT ignored: it is a placeholder-only
# template and README tells the reader to copy it. Ignoring it meant a fresh
# clone received a README pointing at a file it did not have.

# Browser sessions (contain login cookies)
sessions/

# Failure screenshots (capture logged-in account UI — never commit)
debug/
debug_*.png

# Post-run history (contains captions/account activity — local only)
# Glob, not an exact name: backups taken before a prune carry the same
# caption content and must never become committable.
history.jsonl*

# Scheduling queue + per-batch media snapshots (local working state)
queue.jsonl
queue_media/

# Documentation is local-only by default (#50 Phase C, 2026-08-02).
#
# Exactly four markdown documents are public. Everything else — specs, handoff,
# practices, reviewer briefs, workflow lessons, audits, phase closeouts and the
# platform-detection research — stays on the maintainer's disk.
#
# An allowlist, not a list of internal filenames. Enumerating them is what let
# `briefs/` and `workflow-practices/` become committable: the rules named the
# old index files, and a doc split created directories no rule matched. Under
# an allowlist a new internal document is ignored the moment it is created,
# which is the failure mode that put five debug screenshots into history (#60).
#
# Adding a public document therefore takes a deliberate negation line — which
# is the point. `test_documented_long_file_sizes_are_current` and the handoff
# budget test warn-and-skip when their targets are absent, so a fresh clone
# stays green.
*.md
!README.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!ROADMAP.md
!.github/pull_request_template.md

# Non-markdown contents of the internal doc directories.
practices/
workflow-practices/
briefs/
phases/

# Agent tooling is installed from the canonical agentic-workflow plugin.
# Do not commit repo-local skill bundles or machine-specific Claude settings.
.claude/*.skill
.claude/settings.local.json

# Caption styles: allowlist the four generic seed styles, ignore everything
# else in prompts/. Personal styles name real people and tie this repo to the
# accounts it posts to, so they stay local (#50 Phase B, 2026-07-31).
#
# An allowlist rather than naming the personal files: a blocklist would have
# to spell out the names it exists to keep out of the repo. It is also
# stricter — a new personal style is ignored by default instead of needing to
# be remembered. Pinned by test_tracked_prompts_are_exactly_the_seed_set.
prompts/*.json
!prompts/generic.json
!prompts/meme-humor.json
!prompts/sports.json
!prompts/music-fanpage.json

# Uploaded media (temporary)
media/*
!media/.gitkeep

# Coverage artifact — regenerated by every --cov run, was tracked until
# 2026-07-26 and dirtied `git status` on every test run
.coverage

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local-only audit finding reports (directions, not tracked artifacts)
tech-debt-audit.md
